<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<ns0:example xmlns:ns0="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:ns1="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="fs-id1167836683566">
<ns0:exercise id="fs-id1167836561265">
<ns0:problem id="fs-id1167836506912">
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167829681109">Determine whether each equation is a function. Assume <ns1:math><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi></ns1:math> is the independent variable.</ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167833303503"><ns0:span class="token">ⓐ</ns0:span> <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>7</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> <ns0:span class="token">ⓑ</ns0:span> <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:msup><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn></ns1:msup><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>1</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> <ns0:span class="token">ⓒ</ns0:span> <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:msup><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn></ns1:msup><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>3</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math></ns0:para>
</ns0:problem>
<ns0:solution id="fs-id1167836398976">
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167829599793"><ns0:span class="token">ⓐ</ns0:span> <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>7</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math></ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167832926075">For each value of <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis>, we multiply it by <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mn>−2</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> and then add 7 to get the <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">y</ns0:emphasis>-value</ns0:para>
<ns0:table id="fs-id1167836429672" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="y = negative 2 x plus 7. For example, if x = 3. y = negative 2 times 3 plus 7. y = 1.">
<ns0:label />
<ns0:tgroup cols="2">
<ns0:colspec colnum="1" colname="c1" />
<ns0:colspec colnum="2" colname="c2" />
<ns0:tbody>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167836495341" alt="The image displays the linear equation y = -2x + 7, shown in a simple, clear font against a white background.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_010a_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row valign="top">
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left">For example, if <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>3</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>:</ns1:mo><ns1:mspace width="2em" /></ns1:mrow></ns1:math></ns0:entry>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167836619694" alt="The equation y = -2 '.' 3 + 7 is shown, with the number 3 highlighted in red.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_010b_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row valign="top">
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167836326343" alt="The image shows the mathematical equation y = 1 in a bold, sans-serif font on a white background. It represents a horizontal line where the y-coordinate is constant at 1.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_010c_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
</ns0:tbody>
</ns0:tgroup>
</ns0:table>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167833056514">We have that when <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>3</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>,</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> then <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>1</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>.</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> It would work similarly for any value of <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis>. Since each value of <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis>, corresponds to only one value of <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">y</ns0:emphasis> the equation defines a function.</ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836447354"><ns0:span class="token">ⓑ</ns0:span> <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:msup><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn></ns1:msup><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>1</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math></ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167829712213">For each value of <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis>, we square it and then add 1 to get the <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">y</ns0:emphasis>-value.</ns0:para>
<ns0:table id="fs-id1167836533787" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="y = x squared plus 1. For example, if x = 2. y = 2 squared plus 1. y = 5.">
<ns0:label />
<ns0:tgroup cols="2">
<ns0:colspec colnum="1" colname="c1" />
<ns0:colspec colnum="2" colname="c2" />
<ns0:tbody>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167836547666" alt="The equation y = x^2 + 1 is displayed in a mathematical expression. This represents a parabola shifted upwards by one unit on the y-axis, centered at x=0.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_011a_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left">For example, if <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>:</ns1:mo><ns1:mspace width="2em" /></ns1:mrow></ns1:math></ns0:entry>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167836616301" alt="A mathematical equation is displayed on a white background, which reads 'y = 2^2 + 1'. The number 2 in '2^2' is highlighted in red, suggesting it might be the focus of the equation.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_011b_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167836510387" alt="The image displays the mathematical equation 'y = 5' in a clean, straightforward manner on a white background, highlighting a constant value for the variable 'y'.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_011c_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
</ns0:tbody>
</ns0:tgroup>
</ns0:table>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167829936815">We have that when <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>,</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> then <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>5</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>.</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> It would work similarly for any value of <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis>. Since each value of <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis>, corresponds to only one value of <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">y</ns0:emphasis> the equation defines a function.</ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836515845"><ns0:span class="token">ⓒ</ns0:span> <ns0:newline />
<ns0:table id="fs-id1167829596595" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="x plus y squared = 3. Isolate the y term. y squared = negative x plus 3. Let’s substitute x = 2. y squared = negative 2 plus 3. y squared = 1.">
<ns0:label />
<ns0:tgroup cols="2">
<ns0:colspec colnum="1" colname="c1" />
<ns0:colspec colnum="2" colname="c2" />
<ns0:tbody>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167829789899" alt="A mathematical equation is displayed, showing 'x + y^2 = 3' in a clear, dark font against a white background.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_012a_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left">Isolate the <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">y</ns0:emphasis> term.</ns0:entry>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167833356461" alt="The image displays the mathematical equation y^2 = -x + 3, presented in a clear, digital format on a plain white background.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_012b_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left">Let’s substitute <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>.</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math></ns0:entry>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167836618915" alt="A mathematical equation is displayed, showing 'y² = -2 + 3' with the number 2 highlighted in red, indicating a specific part of the calculation.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_012c_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry />
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="left"><ns0:media id="fs-id1167836296194" alt="The mathematical equation y^2 = 1 is displayed in black text on a white background.">
<ns0:image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_IntAlg_Figure_03_05_012d_img.jpg" />
</ns0:media>
</ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
<ns0:row>
<ns0:entry>This give us two values for <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">y</ns0:emphasis>.</ns0:entry>
<ns0:entry valign="top" align="center"><ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>1</ns1:mn><ns1:mspace width="0.2em" /><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>−1</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math></ns0:entry>
</ns0:row>
</ns0:tbody>
</ns0:tgroup>
</ns0:table></ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836539656">We have shown that when <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>2</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>,</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> then <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>1</ns1:mn></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> and <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>−1</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>.</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> It would work similarly for any value of <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis>. Since each value of <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis> does not corresponds to only one value of <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">y</ns0:emphasis> the equation does not define a function.</ns0:para>
</ns0:solution>
</ns0:exercise>
</ns0:example>
